        "paragraph_id": "1C40FC0D",
        "text": "In variation of (2.11), one could also use another wave breaking formulation, presented in (2.12). This formulation is somewhat different than the formulation of Roelvink (1993a) and selected using keyword break=roelvink2. The main difference with the original formulation is that wave dissipation with break=roelvink2 is proportional to H3/h instead of H2."
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 13105,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 364,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 314,
        "paragraph_id": "0C1C6138",
        "text": "Alternatively the formulation of Daly et al. (2010) states that waves are fully breaking if the wave height exceeds a threshold (γ) and stop breaking if the wave height fall below another threshold (γ2). This formulation is selected by break=roelvink_daly and the second threshold, γ2, can be set using keyword: gamma2."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 13185,
